# Database

## Stack: Drizzle + Supabase (Postgres)

Client setup in `src/lib/db.ts`:

```ts
import { drizzle } from "drizzle-orm/postgres-js"
import postgres from "postgres"
import * as schema from "./schema"

const client = postgres(process.env.DATABASE_URL!)
export const db = drizzle(client, { schema })
```

## Schema — Drizzle table definitions

All tables in `src/lib/schema.ts` (or split by domain: `schema/users.ts`, `schema/posts.ts`).

```ts
import { pgTable, text, timestamp, uuid } from "drizzle-orm/pg-core"

export const users = pgTable("users", {
  id: uuid("id").primaryKey().defaultRandom(),
  email: text("email").notNull().unique(),
  name: text("name").notNull(),
  createdAt: timestamp("created_at").notNull().defaultNow(),
  updatedAt: timestamp("updated_at").notNull().defaultNow(),
})

export type User = typeof users.$inferSelect
export type NewUser = typeof users.$inferInsert
```

## Queries — always typed

```ts
// ✅ Select with type inference
const user = await db.select().from(users).where(eq(users.id, id)).limit(1)
// user: { id: string; email: string; name: string; ... }[]

// ✅ Insert returning
const [created] = await db.insert(users).values(newUser).returning()

// ✅ Transaction
await db.transaction(async (tx) => {
  const [user] = await tx.insert(users).values(userData).returning()
  await tx.insert(profiles).values({ userId: user.id, ...profileData })
})

// ❌ Never raw string SQL for user data
db.execute(sql`SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${userId}`) // ok only for dynamic queries
```

## Migrations

Generate: `npx drizzle-kit generate`
Apply: `npx drizzle-kit migrate`

Rules:
- Never edit a migration file after it has been applied
- One migration per feature branch
- Migration names describe what they do: `0001_create_users.sql`
- Always test rollback plan before merging

## Supabase RLS (Row Level Security)

If using Supabase directly from the frontend:
- Enable RLS on every table
- Never disable RLS unless the table is truly public
- Policies live in `supabase/migrations/` as SQL

```sql
-- Users can only read their own rows
CREATE POLICY "users_own_data" ON users
  FOR ALL USING (auth.uid() = id);
```

## Query patterns

```ts
// Pagination
const items = await db.select().from(posts)
  .orderBy(desc(posts.createdAt))
  .limit(20)
  .offset((page - 1) * 20)

// Relations with joins
const postsWithAuthor = await db
  .select({ post: posts, author: users })
  .from(posts)
  .leftJoin(users, eq(posts.authorId, users.id))
  .where(eq(posts.published, true))
```

## Do not

- No `SELECT *` in production queries — select only needed columns
- No synchronous DB calls — always `await`
- No connection pools larger than needed (Supabase pooler handles this)
- No secrets in migration files
